{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Tremble</b> — Because they shamed him instead of honoring him and spoke lies about him, he said: Tremble before HaShem; be afraid — as in: \"Tremble not on the way, for the king asks about his mockers.\" Some say: Since you devise lies in your heart, let them not come out of your mouth — and this is incorrect. It is written: \"He who speaks truth in his heart,\" \"a heart devising wicked schemes\" — and the speech of the heart is the essence, while the tongue is not, except as an interpreter between the heart and the hearers. Rather, the interpretation is: ponder in your heart at night upon your beds, that you have no business with the sons of men, and do not speak lies by day — and this is: \"and be silent, selah.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:23.530945347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}